id.instance: String (TS "c<n>") (not used in this chunk)
num.game: i32 (not used in this chunk; server integers are compared through `as i64`)
num.cursor: u32 (not used in this chunk)
map.ordered: IndexMap
bag.data: IndexMap<String, serde_json::Value> (not used in this chunk)
error.style: Result<_, ApiError> from handlers and grants, Result<_, impl Display> from load_env; panic only on invariants
null.optional: Option + skip_serializing_if
null.nullable: Option, serialised null
case.json: camelCase via serde rename_all (the tests read store rows and bodies as TS's JSON)
case.rust: snake_case
state.mut: &mut GameState writes, &GameState reads, &mut EngineSink for TS sink mutators (not used in this chunk)
rng.source: Rng::new(&state.seed, state.rng_cursor) and write the cursor back (not used in this chunk)
hook.style: Arc<dyn Fn + Send + Sync> via hook(); no fn pointers, no Box (the fake store's on_call is Arc<dyn Fn(&str) -> Result<(), StoreError> + Send + Sync>)
registry.style: OnceLock set once by register_all; fused scripts built on lookup from state (not used in this chunk)
async.style: tokio in crates/server only; none in pure crates; #[tokio::test] current-thread, start_paused for every redemption
log.style: tracing JSON to stdout, server only; tests read events back through a recording tracing_subscriber Layer
test.app: app::load_server_env + app::build under E2E=1, then FakeData::reset() where TS's empty memory store was assumed
test.request: tower::ServiceExt::oneshot over app::router; peer as axum ConnectInfo<SocketAddr>
test.clock: tokio::time paused (padding); wall-clock epoch ms for attempt and grant stamps
